 The exponential pressure-overclosure behavior takes the form in Figure 113 in CCX manual (read pdf file). The parameters c_0 and p_0 define the kind of contact. p_0 is the contact pressure at zero distance, c_0 is the distance from the master surface at which the pressure is decreased to 1 % of p_0. The behavior in between is exponential. A large value of c_0 leads to soft contact, a small value to hard contact. Hard contact gives more accurate results in contact stress values, but soft contact is easier to get convergence.
